1:1 COMMENT "# generator_counter.z -- the smallest generator there is."
1:58 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# `Counter` has no construction state, so it needs no `is` block at"
3:68 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# all: `generator as { ... }` is a complete definition, and the"
4:64 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# three spellings `generator { } as`, `generator as` and"
5:57 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# `generator is {} as` parse to the same thing."
6:48 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "#"
7:2 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# With no fields to fill, its bare name constructs it -- `for x:"
8:65 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# Counter loop` is the zero-argument construction every type gets,"
9:67 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# and `for x: (Counter) loop` is the same thing written out. Both"
10:66 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "# compile to the same C."
11:25 EOL "\n"
12:1 EOL "\n"
